"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is in a mixed initialization state shall be undefined behaviour."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the byte count of the original buffer slice is not a multiple of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the stride of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":", then the re-bound buffer is shorter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than the original buffer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After executing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":", this method rebinds memory back to its original"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binding state. This can be unbound memory, or bound to a different type."}]},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The buffer slice’s start address must match the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alignment of ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (as reported by ","type":"text"},{"code":"MemoryLayout<T>.alignment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). That is,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int(bitPattern: base.baseAddress+startIndex) % MemoryLayout<T>.alignment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must equal zero.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A raw buffer slice may represent memory that has been bound to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a type. If that is the case, then ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" must be layout compatible with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type to which the memory has been bound. This requirement does not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apply if the raw buffer represents memory that has not been bound","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"tex